{{Protection}}{{MagicWords}}

{{Card Infobox|Cost=5|Rarity=Epic|Type=Troop|Arena=Serenity Peak|ReleaseDate=27 January 2017}}{{SubpageNavBox|Evolution=yes|MergeTactics=yes}}{{Quote|He throws his axe like a boomerang, striking all enemies on the way out AND back. It's a miracle he doesn't lose an arm.}}

The Executioner is an {{Rarity|Epic}} [[Cards|card]] that is unlocked from the [[Arenas|Serenity Peak (Arena 14)]]. It spawns an area damage, air-targeting, medium-ranged, ground [[:Category:Troop Cards|troop]] with high hitpoints and high damage. The Executioner launches an axe that travels up to its maximum range, and returns back to him after some time, while piercing through enemies in both ways. He appears as a shirtless man who has blue eyes, a large red nose, a five-o'clock shadow, carries a double-sided axe with a chip on one of its sides, and wears a black mask, gloves and boots, a belt, and a team-colored kilt and pants. An Executioner card costs 5 [[Elixir]] to deploy.

==Modifiers==
===[[File:Executioner Common Modifier.png|45x45px]] Common: Stronger Than Ever===
{{Quote|+100% hitpoints}}
Doubles Executioner hitpoints.

===[[File:Executioner Rare Modifier.png|45x45px]] Rare: Let's Axe a Dud!===
{{Quote|x4 axes}}
Throws 4 axes at a time instead of 1.

===[[File:Executioner Epic Modifier.png|45x45px]] Epic: Axed with the Wind===
{{Quote|Tornado axe}}
Combines the [[Tornado]] spell with its axe attack.

==Strategy==
{{Battle Deck with Card|:Category:Battle Decks using the Executioner Card}}
*The Executioner's long range, ability to hit air [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]], and area damage can allow him to fulfill similar defensive roles to a [[Wizard]], Bowler, [[Witch]], [[Baby Dragon]], or a Bomber.
*Although Executioner's range is 4.5 tiles, his axe throw has a range of 7.5 tiles, and the axe itself has a 1 tile radius, so his effective reach is 8.5 tiles. The defending player should always separate their troops and never deploy them directly in front of their [[:Category:Crown Towers|Crown Tower]], as otherwise they may end up letting the Executioner deal substantial chip damage.
*His hit speed comes in two parts; 0.9 seconds to throw his axe and 1.5 seconds for his axe to return. This adds up to an overall 2.4-second hit speed. [[Rage]] and slowing effects will only affect how long it takes the axe to return to his hand, which will be evened out by Executioner throwing the axe slower. Therefore, damage per second does not make a difference. Even when he's pulled backwards by the [[Tornado]], the axe will still take 1.5 seconds to return.
*Due to being [[:Category:Spell Cards|spell]] resistant and having decent damage per swing, the Executioner is great against low to medium health troops. However, his damage per second is somewhat low for 5 [[Elixir]], so mini tanks such as the [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Lumberjack]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Knight]], [[Dark Prince]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Battle Healer]], and [[Prince]] can easily counter him.
*High-damage ranged troops like the [[Musketeer]], Wizard, [[Inferno Dragon]], or [[Electro Wizard]] are decent counters to a lone Executioner. They typically have higher damage per second and range than the Executioner, allowing them to get decent damage on him before he deals too much back to them. With the help of any tower troop, they can stop him for positive Elixir trades, and some may even survive for a counterattack.
*Left alone, the Executioner will deal the same damage to all [[:Category:Tower Troop Cards|tower troops]], throwing his axe 3 times against all of them. It is most recommended to lower this with a cheap distraction first to lower any damage dealt to the Crown Tower.
*The [[P.E.K.K.A.]] works quite well with the Executioner because he can deal area damage that can help defend against swarms, while the P.E.K.K.A. strikes down tanks with her massively high DPS.
*The [[Rocket]] is able to instantly destroy the Executioner for a -1 Elixir trade. This can be quite advantageous if he is placed at the back, allowing the player to hit both the Crown Tower and the Executioner. However, the player can take advantage of the lack of a Rocket and deploy something that would thrive from its absence, such as a [[Sparky]].
*The range of the Executioner's axe lets him not only damage a tank like the [[Giant]], but also being able to hit support troops behind the tank if the Executioner is placed aligned with the enemy tank.
*The Tornado spell works well with the Executioner. The Tornado can group enemy troops together, allowing him to easily hit them all.
**Conversely, the Tornado can also be used to defend against the Executioner. Placing the Tornado staggered a tile towards the approaching Executioner and a tile towards the closest [[Arenas|Arena]] wall on the defender’s Crown Tower will cause the Executioner to be pulled diagonally beside the Tower, causing his axe to hit the [[King's Tower|King Tower]] when thrown. However, as this strategy causes unnecessary Tower damage, the Tornado player should contemplate whether a King Tower activation is necessary for them to win, such as if the opponent uses a [[Graveyard]] [[Battle Decks|deck]]. Alternatively, they can allow the Executioner to hit an [[Ice Spirit]] first, and then pull him with the Tornado to minimize Tower damage
*The Executioner is also an excellent counter to swarms of all kinds, capable of defeating most low-cost units with one throw of his axe. However, his low hit speed and directional area damage attack leave him vulnerable to being surrounded by [[Barbarians]], [[Minion Horde]], [[Bats]], [[Skeleton Army]], [[Royal Recruits]], or [[Goblin Gang]] once he crosses the river.
*Like the [[Bowler]], the Executioner's axe continually denies the area that it occupies; troops played on top of it will instantly be damaged. Against cards with a death spawn, like a [[Goblin Hut]] or a [[Tombstone]], a single attack will be able to completely wipe it out.
**This makes him a great counter to the [[Goblin Drill]]. He has high hitpoints to tank a few hits from the [[Goblins]], and his attack will hit the spawned Goblins after the Goblin Drill is destroyed, with the returning hit of the axe finishing off the death Goblins. It is a negative Elixir trade, but this sets him up for a counterattack.
*The Executioner paired with the Prince is a high-risk, high reward strategy. The Prince can take out mini tanks such as the Mini P.E.K.K.A with his charge, while the Executioner can take out swarms such as Bats, Minion Horde, Goblin Gang or Skeleton Army. However, the combo is countered by separating the duo, since they have different movement speeds and ranges.
*When the Goblins of a [[Goblin Barrel]] surround a Crown Tower, an Executioner placed directly behind the Tower will target the Goblin at the back of the Tower aligned to the center, allowing him to damage all three Goblins at once.
*With the help of the [[Tower Princess]], the Executioner can stop a [[Balloon]] for a neutral Elixir trade. His damage is enough to stop all damage from the Balloon, except from the death bomb.
*He is a decent counter to the [[Lava Hound]]; his high damage lets him defeat the Lava Hound and his splash makes him a great choice against the Lava Pups. If timed right, the fatal hit on the Lava Hound will allow the Executioner to hit all Lava Pups at once, preventing even more damage on the Crown Tower.
*If he is defeated while his axe is not in his hand, the axe will still fly back to where he was defeated and inflict damage normally. This is important to know when to drop additional troops to defend against other troops that are supported by the Executioner and avoid unnecessary damage.
*A full throw of the Executioner's axe is enough to eliminate Goblins, [[Minions]], all Spirit [[cards]], [[Princess]], and [[Dart Goblin]] up to 2 Levels higher, [[Archers]] and [[Firecracker|Firecarcker]] up to 1 Level higher, and [[Wall Breakers]] and [[Bomber]] of the same Level. One hit from the axe is enough to OHKO [[Skeletons]], [[Bats]], and [[Spear Goblins]].
*The [[Fisherman]] can be used to activate the King’s Tower against the Executioner. The defender should place the Fisherman in the middle of their side of the Arena, staggered 2 tiles diagonally towards the Crown Tower in the lane that the Executioner is walking in, as soon as the opponent’s Executioner crosses the bridge. The Executioner would then be hooked towards the Fisherman and start firing, with his axe piercing through the Fisherman and activating the King Tower.
*The [[Magic Archer]] is very similar to the Executioner, except that he attacks faster, has less hitpoints, deals less damage, attacks from further, and hits less units due to small splash radius. However, he costs less Elixir, making him more individually flexible compared to the Executioner (i.e. they are not forced to use 5 Elixir on a single push as opposed to dropping 4 Elixir and having an additional 1 Elixir for a second push or a different card altogether).
*When the Executioner's axe hits the [[Monk]] under Pensive Protection, it is immediately returned to him and will cause him to throw it faster and therefore, take lots of damage or otherwise die because of it.

